# AIP escalation patterns — commands that require human approval
# (spec §"Human escalation shims"). One Python regex per line, matched against
# the full command context. A match writes a workspace/gates/gate-*.json record
# and blocks the agent until a human (or the orchestrator) sets approved: true.
#
# Unlike .aip/block (auto-deny), these are NOT denied outright — they pause for
# a human decision. Use for high-consequence but legitimate actions.

# Pushing or deploying to shared/remote targets
git\s+push\b
gh\s+pr\s+create\b
gh\s+pr\s+merge\b

# Deployments and releases
\bdeploy\b
\bpublish\b
npm\s+publish\b
\bterraform\s+apply\b
kubectl\s+apply\b

# Production-scoped operations
--prod\b
--production\b
